meta {
  name: Import Space Repo (Custos)
  type: http
  seq: 163
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/space/import-repo?space={{spaceUri}}
  body: binary
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessJwt}}
}

params:query {
  space: {{spaceUri}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/vnd.ipld.car
}

body:binary {
  @file: {{spaceRepoCarFilePath}}
}

vars:pre-request {
  baseUrl: http://localhost:8080
  spaceUri: at://did:plc:authority/space/org.example.bucket/main
  spaceRepoCarFilePath: ./space-repo.car
}

docs {
  Ingest the two-root CAR exported by com.atproto.space.getRepo into the authenticated
  account's repo in the named space — the permissioned-data leg of account migration.

  Custos-native (/v1/*) rather than a com.atproto.space.* method: the Atproto Spaces alpha
  lexicons define no import endpoint.

  The account must be deactivated, as for com.atproto.repo.importRepo. The repo becomes
  exactly the CAR's record set: records the CAR's index does not name are removed in the same
  commit, so a return migration cannot leave a previous residency behind. Blobs are not
  carried — enumerate them on the source with com.atproto.space.listBlobs and transfer them
  with uploadBlob. If this host is to be the space's authority, recreate the simplespace
  config and member list with createSpace/addMember.

  The destination's oplog starts fresh: syncers holding a `since` from the old host fold to a
  set hash that will not match the new head, which is their signal to heal with a full
  getRepo.

  Returns 200 { rev, records }.
}
